 R←Test_AAA_001(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;filename;data;start;end;injected;current
⍝ Checks that the "List" injected into the user command script, and the file `UC/List.aplf`,
⍝ really are what `UC.List` currently is. When this fails then `#.APLGit2.Admin.Make 1` was
⍝ not run since `UC.List` last changed, and the script therefore advertises other commands - or
⍝ other "Parse" strings - than the source does. Note that this cannot be noticed at runtime:
⍝ `Name`, `Desc` and "Parse" always come from the script, no matter what DEVELOPMENT says.\\
⍝ ATTENTION: this test is named "AAA_001" for a reason: it must run FIRST. When the build is out
⍝ of step with the source, the user command tests fail as well, but with symptoms that point
⍝ anywhere but here - "Counter.aplf not found" rather than "run Make". Do not rename it.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 filename←##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/APLSource/APLGit2_uc.dyalog'
 data←⊃⎕NGET filename 1
 start←⍸∨/¨'⍝ >>>>> StartListInject'∘⍷¨data
 end←⍸∨/¨'⍝ >>>>> EndListInject'∘⍷¨data
 →T.PassesIf 1 1≡(≢start)(≢end)
 injected←1↓(⊃start)↓(¯1+⊃end)↑data          ⍝ 1↓ : that is the MinimumVersionOfDyalog line
 current←1↓G.UC.⎕NR'List'                    ⍝ 1↓ : that is the header
 →T.PassesIf current≡injected
 ⍝ The file must match as well: that is what `BuildPackage` puts into the package
 filename←##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/APLSource/APLGit2/UC/List.aplf'
 →T.PassesIf current≡1↓⊃⎕NGET filename 1

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
